  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I would love to create a matchmaking/game hub world, where users can meet up with each other. It would be great if there was a way, using Udon, to drop a portal to a specified world ID, with the specified instance type, at a specified position and rotation.\nI suppose it would be just like dropping a portal manually-- it simply does not get created if it's in an invalid position (too close to spawn or another player).\nWhy not just drop a portal using the menu? Because it would be a nice shortcut to integrate it into the world somehow, like with a button or animation.\nWhy not just use a normal portal? Those put you in public instances, and I would love to have the same target instance consistency as dropping an invite-only portal manually.",
